# These vendor motion CSVs are committed as RAW blobs (the repo has no actual
# git-lfs objects anywhere), but the package-level .gitattributes marks *.csv
# as lfs — on machines with git-lfs configured that mismatch makes every CSV
# here show as permanently "modified" and git prints "should have been
# pointers, but weren't" on checkout. Deepest .gitattributes wins: unset the
# lfs filtering so the raw blobs are handled as the plain text files they are.
*.csv -filter -diff -merge
